<br/>
<br/>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">The pre-raid best-in-slot set is very close to a carbon copy of the best-in-slot set, but with the <b>LFR</b> variants of items obtained in <b>
<span class="c9">Twilight Protocol</span></b> dungeons. <i>Since it will be a while before you can buy all of the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items, I've only included the most important <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items in the set; when it becomes possible to buy more, I will add more - such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77116/rotting-skull">
<img alt="Rotting Skull" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_orcskull_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rotting Skull</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77110/ring-of-torn-flesh">
<img alt="Ring of Torn Flesh" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_ahnqiraj_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Torn Flesh</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77185/demonbone-waistguard">
<img alt="Demonbone Waistguard" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_plate_raiddeathknight_k_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demonbone Waistguard</span></a>.  </i>
<br/>
<span class="small-text">
<i>If you are a Human or Draenei and need to drop hit due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> or drop expertise due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20597/sword-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_meleedamage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sword Specialization</span></a>, simply reforge your gear to decrease them and get as close to your caps as possible. </i></span></div>
<br/>
<br/>Paladins will focus primarily on melee damage-dealing statistics like Strength, Hit, Expertise, Mastery, Critical Strike, and Haste. You will need to reach the cap for hit chance and expertise to ensure that your attacks are not dodged or miss, causing a loss of potential Holy Power and damage. <i>For more information on this, check out <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/paladin/retribution/dps-stat-priority-attributes-pve">our Retribution Stat Priority Guide</a>. For information on enchanting &amp; gemming your gear, check out <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/paladin/retribution/dps-enchants-gems-pve">our Retribution Enchants &amp; Gems guide</a></i>.<br/>
<br/>You will always be aiming to equip plate items in order to continue to benefit from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86525/plate-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Plate Specialization</span></a>, gaining 5% extra Strength. In general, the item with the highest item level tends to be the strongest; though not strictly true 100% of the time, it is very rare for lower level items to perform better - mostly due to the reforging system. <br/>
<br/>The <b>Raid Finder</b>, also known as "<b>Looking for Raid</b>" (LFR), will not be coming along for the ride in Phase 4. Instead, Blizzard has created a new currency - <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> - and a new dungeon difficulty - <b>
<span class="c9">Twilight Protocol</span></b> - that will reward players with the items that were originally from the <b>LFR</b> system, therefore allowing you to create an extremely powerful pre-raid set. <br/>
<br/>There are also three new dungeons in Phase 4 - <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5788/well-of-eternity">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Well of Eternity</span></a>, <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5789/end-time">
<span class="tinyicontxt">End Time</span></a>, and <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5844/hour-of-twilight">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Hour of Twilight</span></a> - that reward players with the high-level epic gear.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Retribution Paladin DPS in Phase 4</h3>Here is our recommended priority for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> purchases:<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
