<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Retribution Paladin DPS</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="two-handed-weapons-for-retribution-paladin-dps">Two-Handed Weapons for Retribution Paladin DPS</h4>
<i>Slower weapons tend to be stronger than faster weapons of the same item level, with 0.2 slower speed being typically <i>(not always)</i> worth about 9 extra item levels. Slower weapons do more damage because seals and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85256/templars-verdict">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_templarsverdict.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Templar's Verdict</span></a> are not normalized.</i>
<br/>
<br/>Everyone should aim to get <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78487/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a>, which is the <b>LFR</b> variant of our best-in-slot weapon, and drops from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5088/the-stonecore">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Stonecore</span></a> on <b>
<span class="c9">Twilight Protocol</span></b> difficulty - or can be purchased for 100x <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>. It has a 2% chance to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=109840/summon-tentacle-of-the-old-ones">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterhorn_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Summon Tentacle of the Old Ones</span></a> and spawn a <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=58078/tentacle-of-the-old-ones">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Tentacle of the Old Ones</span></a> that hits pretty hard, and since there is no internal cooldown, you can get very lucky and spawn multiple tentacles; providing extremely high DPS if you are lucky enough. Unfortunately, it cannot trigger from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=31801/seal-of-truth">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_sealofvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Truth</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>Only slightly worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78487/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a> is the 384 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71352/sulfuras-the-extinguished-hand">
<img alt="Sulfuras, the Extinguished Hand" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_sulfuras_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sulfuras, the Extinguished Hand</span></a>, which has a cheaper <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> cost, but you should really save them up instead for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78487/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>The only other competitive pre-raid weapon is the PvP greatsword - <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=73475/cataclysmic-gladiators-greatsword">
<img alt="Cataclysmic Gladiator's Greatsword" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_pvpcataclysms3_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cataclysmic Gladiator's Greatsword</span></a> - which, again, only requires an hour or two in the arena earning <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=390/conquest-points">
<span>
<img alt="Conquest Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvpcurrency-conquest-horde.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conquest Points</span></span></a>. There is, of course, the higher level version <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=73442/cataclysmic-gladiators-greatsword">
<img alt="Cataclysmic Gladiator's Greatsword" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_pvpcataclysms3_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cataclysmic Gladiator's Greatsword</span></a> that requires 2200 rating, but this also requires owning the lower-level version first, so in total you effectively need 6800x <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=390/conquest-points">
<span>
<img alt="Conquest Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvpcurrency-conquest-horde.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Conquest Points</span></span></a>, which means that you will not be able to get this in one week, even if you had the rating - but if you can get it, it is the best pre-raid weapon, even above <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78487/gurthalak-voice-of-the-deeps">
<img alt="Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurthalak, Voice of the Deeps</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>There are also two weapons from the new dungeons - <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=72844/pit-lords-destroyer">
<img alt="Pit Lord's Destroyer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_430nightelf_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pit Lord's Destroyer</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=72814/axe-of-the-tauren-chieftains">
<img alt="Axe of the Tauren Chieftains" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_2h_430future_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Axe of the Tauren Chieftains</span></a>, both are solid, with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=72844/pit-lords-destroyer">
<img alt="Pit Lord's Destroyer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_2h_430nightelf_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pit Lord's Destroyer</span></a> being the stronger of the two due to the Mastery. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63679/reclaimed-ashkandi-greatsword-of-the-brotherhood">
<img alt="Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_50.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reclaimed Ashkandi, Greatsword of the Brotherhood</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64377/zinrokh-destroyer-of-worlds">
<img alt="Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_zinrokh-sword.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zin'rokh, Destroyer of Worlds</span></a>, both equivalent, are pretty mediocre at this point.<div class="pad"></div>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74246/enchant-weapon-landslide">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Landslide</span></a>
